{{!
    @template format_aicourse/add_section_card

    The "Add section" card that closes the AI Course section grid. It is a real <button> so it is
    keyboard reachable, and it is only rendered for a teacher with edit mode turned on. Its
    decorative plus icon carries aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"; the visible label is the
    button's accessible name.

    Classes required for JS:
    * aicourse-add-section-card - click handler in amd/src/courseformat.js.

    Data attributes required for JS:
    * data-courseid - the course the new section is added to.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * courseid int Course ID.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "courseid": 2
    }
}}
<button type="button" class="aicourse-add-section-card" data-courseid="{{courseid}}">
<div class="aicourse-add-section-icon"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="16"/><line x1="8" y1="12" x2="16" y2="12"/></svg></div>
<span class="aicourse-add-section-label">{{#str}} addsection, format_aicourse {{/str}}</span>
</button>
